{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>The three cities across the Jordan and the three cities in the land of Canaan.</b> And in the second chapter of Makkot it raises the difficulty: across the Jordan three and in the land of Israel three? And it answers: in Gilead, which is across the Jordan, murderers are common, as it is written: ״גלעד קרית פועלי און עקובה מדם״. Rabbi Elazar said: they would lie in wait to kill persons. And the difficulty is: what is it answering? For cities of refuge avail only for unintentional killers, whereas in Gilead, where murderers are common, that means intentional ones. And one may answer: since intentional murderers are common there, the Holy One, blessed be He, brings unintentional murderers there without witnesses, so that the intentional murderers will be killed there and there will be witnesses and they will go into exile, as we say there shortly: ״מרשעים יצא רשע״ — about what does the verse speak? About two men who killed a person: one killed unintentionally and one killed intentionally. To this one there are no witnesses and to that one there are no witnesses. The Holy One, blessed be He, arranges them at one inn. This one who killed intentionally sits under the ladder, and this one who killed unintentionally climbs the ladder and falls upon him and kills him, and there are witnesses there: this one is killed and that one goes into exile."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:34.046999609Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}